#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference documentation for the home interface, which lets snaps access non-"
"hidden files and directories in the user's home directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:8
msgid "home interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `home` {ref}`interface <explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>` "
"allows access to non-hidden files owned by the user in the user's home "
"($HOME) directory where a user normally stores their personal files and "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The majority of snaps use {ref}`strict confinement <interfaces-install-"
"modes>` and do not have arbitrary access a system's resources, including "
"file and directories in the _\\/home_ directory. Without this access, _home_ "
"will not be visible in file requesters, or as a destination from within the "
"snap application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"To check whether a snap can connect to $HOME, use the _snap connections_ "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"$ snap connections <snap-name>\n"
"Interface  Plug                Slot         Notes\n"
"home       <snap-name>:home    -        -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"The above output shows that `<snap-name>` does provide a home interface (in "
"the _Plug_ column), but that it's not connected to any slot (denoted by the "
"`-` in the slot column)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:24
msgid "Use the _snap connect_ command to connect an interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:26
msgid "$ snap connect <snap-name>:home :home\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"The `:home` slot, with no \\<snap-name\\>  before the colon (`:`) is "
"equivalent to directing the plug to connect to the system, which in this "
"case is the $HOME directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"A snap developer can {ref}`request permission <interfaces-process-for-"
"aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` to have the `home` interface connected "
"automatically. In this case, non-hidden files and directories will be "
"accessible from that snap without any further configuration being necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:33
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.33+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:35
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:37
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-Connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:38
msgid "**yes** on traditional distributions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:39
msgid ""
"**no** on all other systems, including {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-"
"glossary_ubuntu-core>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:41
msgid "**Transitional**: yes</br> **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:41
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/home-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"`read` (plug): optional, when set to 'all', also allows reading non-hidden "
"files in the home directories of all users as traditional file permissions "
"allow. _When set to 'all' this plug becomes non-autoconnect._"
msgstr ""

